Resolutions
8.
Consideration of a resolution to prohibit open carry for all county
buildings and facilities, effective July 15, 2025.
25 - 320
Resolution, Prohibit Open Carry for All County
Buildings and Facilities
Attachments:
County Attorney Mark Voss explained there were recent changes in state law
regarding conceal carry and open carry of firearms.  He said the law gives
municipalities and counties the ability to prohibit open carry in and on governmental
property.  He said the resolution is a proposition to prohibit open carry in and on
county property.
Commissioner Thompson said he did not see a good reason to prohibit open carry.
Commissioner Hollingshead said the prohibition would cause undue angst to people
and would be challenged by certain groups.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, that this agenda item be approved. The
motion failed by the following vote:
