Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
July 15, 2025
In response to a questions from commissioners about levels of home occupations and
small tiered marketing businesses, Arnold explained that home occupations are not
intended to have retail sales open to the public.  He said businesses open to the
public will have a site plan, and the proposed regulations allow flexibility for whatever
people might be doing on their property.   He added home occupations are online, by
phone, or by appointment.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, that this agenda item be postponed until August
5, 2025. The motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
