```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
July 15, 2025
venue with an outdoor paintball field and axe throwing. Arnold said Laramie County
Land Use Regulations identifies entertainment and recreation facilities as a use by
right in the CB zone district.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT.
Ryan Cox, State Engineers' office, said the well needs to brought up to statute and
regulations.  He recommended the applicant work with his office to ensure everything
is in order.
Arnold said the State Engineer can be included on the site plan review, and informed
the board there was no need for an additional condition.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Zwonitzer, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, to approve the zone change from AR to CB
for a portion of  Section 36, Township 14 North, Range 66 West, Laramie
County, WY, with no conditions, and adopt the findings of fact a and b of
the staff report. The motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
13. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a subdivision permit and plat for Archer
Estates, 12th Filing, located at Tract 1, Archer Estates, 9th Filing,
Laramie County, WY.
25 - 313
Archer Estates, 12th Filing, Subdivision Permit and
Plat
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Jones Land Surveying, Inc, on behalf of Carl L and
Debra K Smith, submitted an application for approval of a subdivision permit and plat
for Archer Estates, 12th Filing, located at Tract 1, Archer Estates, 9th Filing, Laramie
County, WY. The proposed subdivision will create two (2) residential tracts from the
parcel.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT.
Ryan Cox, State Engineer's office, noted the subdivision will be in the Laramie County
control area, conservation area, one water right attached to the entire land.  He said
the applicant needs the water rights attached to the proper tract of the land, and if
there is a new well, the approved permit will be issued through the State Engineer's
office.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
